INSERT INTO blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, category, tags, status, author, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('average-calculator-guide', 'Average Calculator: how it works, formula and examples', 'Average Calculator: Mean, median, mode and range of a list. Learn how to use it, the formula behind it, a worked example and answers to common questions.', 'The [Average Calculator](/average-calculator) is a free online tool on CalcHub. Mean, median, mode and range of a list. Enter your numbers (comma or space separated) and the result appears straight away — no account or download needed. Because it runs entirely in your browser, the values you type never leave your device, and you can use it as often as you like.

The average (arithmetic mean) is the sum of values divided by how many there are. Median and mode give a fuller picture when data has outliers. This guide explains how to use it, the formula it applies, and a worked example you can follow with your own numbers. Related Math tools include [Percentage Calculator](/percentage-calculator), [Fraction Calculator](/fraction-calculator) and [Square Root Calculator](/square-root-calculator).

## How to use the Average Calculator

