INSERT INTO blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, category, tags, status, author, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('circle-calculator-guide', 'Circle Calculator: how it works, formula and examples', 'Circle Calculator: Area, circumference and diameter from a circle''s radius. Learn how to use it, the formula behind it, a worked example and answers to common…', 'The [Circle Calculator](/circle-calculator) is a free online tool on CalcHub. Area, circumference and diameter from a circle''s radius. Enter your radius and the result appears straight away — no account or download needed. Because it runs entirely in your browser, the values you type never leave your device, and you can use it as often as you like. It is one of the [Math tools](/tools?category=Math) on CalcHub — the others work the same way.

Area, circumference and diameter from a circle''s radius. This free online circle calculator gives you an instant answer without an account, a download or sending your entries to a server. It is designed for quick everyday use on desktop and mobile. This guide explains how to use it, the formula it applies, and a worked example you can follow with your own numbers.

## How to use the Circle Calculator

