- [Weight Converter](/weight-converter)
- [Area Converter](/area-converter)
- [Browse all Conversion tools](/tools?category=Conversion)
- [More guides](/blog)', 'Conversion', ARRAY['Conversion', 'fps converter', 'frames per second converter', 'fps to ms converter'], 'published', 'CalcHub', '2026-11-20T03:24:43.059Z', '2026-11-21T12:38:31.138Z') ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, content = EXCLUDED.content, category = EXCLUDED.category, tags = EXCLUDED.tags, status = EXCLUDED.status, author = EXCLUDED.author, updated_at = EXCLUDED.updated_at;
INSERT INTO blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, category, tags, status, author, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('fraction-calculator-guide', 'Fraction Calculator: how it works, formula and examples', 'Fraction Calculator: Add, subtract, multiply and divide fractions. Learn how to use it, the formula behind it, a worked example and answers to common questions.', 'The [Fraction Calculator](/fraction-calculator) is a free online tool on CalcHub. Add, subtract, multiply and divide fractions. Enter your numerator 1, denominator 1, operation, numerator 2 and denominator 2 and the result appears straight away — no account or download needed. Because it runs entirely in your browser, the values you type never leave your device, and you can use it as often as you like.

A fraction calculator performs arithmetic on fractions and reduces the answer to its simplest form, with mixed-number and decimal equivalents. This guide explains how to use it, the formula it applies, and a worked example you can follow with your own numbers. Related Math tools include [Percentage Calculator](/percentage-calculator), [Square Root Calculator](/square-root-calculator) and [Average Calculator](/average-calculator). People also look for this tool as "adding fractions calculator", "simplify fractions", "fraction to decimal".

