a/b + c/d = (ad + bc)/bd. a/b × c/d = ac/bd. a/b ÷ c/d = ad/bc. Simplify by dividing by the greatest common divisor. You can see it in action in the [Fraction Calculator](/fraction-calculator) — enter your own values and the result updates as you type.

### What do I need to use the Fraction Calculator?

Just Numerator 1, Denominator 1, Operation, Numerator 2 and Denominator 2. Enter those values and the result appears straight away — no account or download needed. If you are unsure about a value, try a rough figure first and then refine it — the result updates instantly.

## Related tools

If this calculation is part of a bigger job, the other Math tools on CalcHub can help. The [Percentage Calculator](/percentage-calculator), [Square Root Calculator](/square-root-calculator), [Average Calculator](/average-calculator) and [Standard Deviation Calculator](/standard-deviation-calculator) all work the same way — enter your values and the result appears instantly, free and with no sign-up. For more detail, read the guides to the [Percentage Calculator](/blog/percentage-calculator-guide) and [Square Root Calculator](/blog/square-root-calculator-guide), which explain how those calculations work and when to use them.

