- [More guides](/blog)', 'Finance', ARRAY['Finance', 'refinance calculator', 'mortgage refinance calculator', 'refinance break even'], 'published', 'CalcHub', '2026-11-17T19:11:25.562Z', '2026-11-21T12:38:31.138Z') ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, content = EXCLUDED.content, category = EXCLUDED.category, tags = EXCLUDED.tags, status = EXCLUDED.status, author = EXCLUDED.author, updated_at = EXCLUDED.updated_at;
INSERT INTO blog_posts (slug, title, excerpt, content, category, tags, status, author, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('regex-tester-guide', 'Regex Tester: how it works, formula and examples', 'Regex Tester: Test a JavaScript regular expression and list every match. Learn how to use it, the formula behind it, a worked example and answers to common…', 'The [Regex Tester](/regex-tester) is a free online tool on CalcHub. Test a JavaScript regular expression and list every match. Enter your regular expression, flags and test text and the result appears straight away — no account or download needed. Because it runs entirely in your browser, the values you type never leave your device, and you can use it as often as you like.

Test a JavaScript regular expression and list every match. This free online regex tester gives you an instant answer without an account, a download or sending your entries to a server. It is designed for quick everyday use on desktop and mobile. This guide explains how to use it, the formula it applies, and a worked example you can follow with your own numbers.

