With the default values (Price: 100, Sales tax rate: 8.25 %, Price entered is: Before tax), the [Sales Tax Calculator](/sales-tax-calculator) returns Total with tax: 108.25, Tax amount: 8.25, Price before tax: 100. The first figure is the headline result, and the rest break it down so you can see how the total is made up. Change any value and every figure updates instantly. If you want to compare with a related calculation, the [Loan Calculator](/loan-calculator) is worth a look before you finish.

## Tips

A few things worth knowing before you rely on the result — most of them are about the numbers you put in, rather than the tool itself:

- Rates vary by state, county and city in the US.
- Some items, like groceries, may be exempt.

Keep these in mind and the figures will be as useful as the numbers you put in.

## Frequently asked questions

### How do I calculate sales tax backwards?

Divide the total by 1 plus the tax rate as a decimal — e.g. total ÷ 1.0825 for 8.25%. Try it with your own numbers in the [Sales Tax Calculator](/sales-tax-calculator) — the result updates as you type, so you can test a few scenarios in seconds.

### Is sales tax charged on discounts?

Usually tax applies to the price after a store discount. Try it with your own numbers in the [Sales Tax Calculator](/sales-tax-calculator) — the result updates as you type, so you can test a few scenarios in seconds.

